writing simple examples that explain what each step is.
Part of it is that any real example requires a whole load
of boilerplate to get off the ground.

> Anyway, would it maybe make sense to have the generated model code catch all exceptions and then update the message by including line numbers?

That's a great idea.  I'd have to wrap all the code that calls statements
with try/catches to do that, including each function, the constructor,
the log probability function, and some of the write functions that bring
in generated quantities.  But that should be much more robust.

