I don't know much about exactly how exceptions are caught (but
I can swot up on it).

Does anyone know if the following will work and allow the
catch to be keyed of the type E?

  template <typename E>
  located_exception : public E {
    const T& e_;
    const int begin_;
    const int end_;
    located_exception(const E& e, int begin, int end)
    : e_(e), begin_(begin), end_(end) { }
  };

The simpler option is this:

  located_exception : std::exception {
    const std::exception& e_;
    const int begin_;
    const int end_;

    located_exception(std::exception E& e, int begin, int end)
    : e_(e), begin_(begin), end_(end) { }

  };

- Bob

