Sorry for all the fragmented mail.  I just read that link and see this:

  As of gcc 4.3, a quadruple precision is also supported on x86, but as
  the nonstandard type __float128 rather than long double.

Damn that GCC.  I thought only Microsoft went off the rails like this.

Has anyone tried updating Eigen to see what the behvior is?

Or does anyone know how to test for GCC >= 4.3 and include
a definition for long double?

I can't get the enable_if stuff to work on Windows generally
enough, but we may have to go back to trying this route.

C++ is just a nightmare with all this non-standard crap flying
around.

- Bob

