Jonathan:

Would you mind dropping this into src/stan/math/rev/core/var.hpp
and see if it compiles:

  var(__float128 x) : vi_(new vari(static_cast<double>(x))) { }

If so, we'll work on getting the #ifdef GCC 4.3 or greater into
place to wrap it (I'm still not sure what the preferred way of
doing that is.)  Who knew that GCC had the same cowboy mentality
as Windows!

Also, if you could somehow turn off libquadmath, that would
probably work, too.  I see it being brought in with this:

  boost_1.55.0/boost/multiprecision/float128.hpp:#include <quadmath.h>
  boost_1.55.0/boost/multiprecision/float128.hpp:      int v = quadmath_snprintf (buf, 100, format.c_str(), digits, m_value);
  boost_1.55.0/boost/multiprecision/float128.hpp:         v = quadmath_snprintf (&buf2[0], v_max + 3, format.c_str(), digits, m_value);

Oddly, I don't see any other library file in boost
that includes it, so I'm not sure how it's getting into
our code.

Thanks,

- Bob

