Looks wrong to me, which is why I wrote into the Eigen list
in the first place.

I checked and the problem persists in Eigen 3.2.4.  It seems
like if we add -DEIGEN2_SUPPORT we'll get a compiler warning, but
things will work, and if we then add -DEIGEN_NO_EIGEN2_DEPRECATED_WARNING,
it'll turn off that compiler warning.  What a mess!

Ditto the efficient detection of NaN, which looks like it'll have
to wait until C++11.

- Bob

