The only way to have an R-like experience would be to have multiple naming conventions in the spirit of 'read.table' which blesses R with a combination of col.names/nrows/stringsAsFactors in the arguments.  Maybe optimize.bfgs and optimize.lbfgs versus sampleHMC and sampleNUTS. In addition you would need at last two perpetually-coexisting ways of defining functions in Stan, preferably three.  Also all error messages would be some variant of "Error in FUN(X[[1L]], ...) : subscript out of bounds".  Nothing would ever be deprecated.  Please save us from the R-like experience.

Krzysztof

