I think it’s important to remember that because none of the
interfaces use command nothing in this branch has a huge
effect on anything but CmdStan so any related comments
are irrelevant.

Seriously, though, this is becoming a problem.  Allen essentially
wants a C-interface which is a gigantic change to our current
setup, including the perspective of Stan as a C++ API on the
whole.  I’m not even sure what Jiqiang is advocating, but
the whole point of a unified UX is that the interfaces _don’t_
get to do whatever they want.  We’re getting dangerously
close to every interface being completely independent, and
once that happens we lose a tremendous potential for Stan.

