Hi everyone,

I find Bob's edits really helpful.

The goal of increasing code reuse trumps my concerns about C++ and
callbacks. While I'm still strongly in favor of reducing the amount of C++
code that needs to be maintained from the R and Python side, if we can
get some shared way of validating and populating-with-defaults the
proposed "stan::command::config" instance, then I'll be happy. Sharing rhat
and ess calculations would be next on the list.

I also support breaking up the interface into different functions
(lbfgs, hmc, ...) -- to what extent does this overlap with the RStan
Wiki discussion
https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/Interfaces-3.0-Spec?

Thanks,

-a

