> I’m not even sure what Jiqiang is advocating, but
> the whole point of a unified UX is that the interfaces _don’t_
> get to do whatever they want.

I agree --- everything should be unified.  But I think
we should design with the interfaces in mind --- they're how
almost everyone uses Stan, so getting the interfaces right
is important.

> We’re getting dangerously
> close to every interface being completely independent, and
> once that happens we lose a tremendous potential for Stan.

I think the key thing is that the language stays the same
and that the interfaces look relatively natural from their
host languages and that we use common computations in Stan C++
for all the heavy lifting.

Everything else is a detail.

- Bob

