Double* is preferable. Double* is the internal representation used by
Python (NumPy) anyway and I suspect it's the same for R. So if you pass
a vector it will have to be converted to double* anyway.

In fact, double* is better because there's no uncertainty about memory
contiguity from the interface's side (IIRC).

Thanks,

Allen

